summary:
  While an alarm rings every verdict doubles the wait before the next one.

history:
  Bench, 2026-11-12: an alarm's station gave every connection 8 s of
  sound and then held it open. The verdicts came 5, 10 and 20 s after the
  player's error, and the silences between the 8 s of station grew from
  31 s to 66 s and past 85 s, with a sleeper to wake.

target:
  package/contents/ui/StandLogic.js

find:
      if (waking === true) n = 0;

replace:
      if (waking === null) n = 0;

expect:
  Killed by tst_standlogic::test_while_an_alarm_rings_no_verdict_lengthens_the_wait.
  Line-neutral.
